/-!
# Column-side enumeration for `q = 1`: `H'`-cosets — data and boolean certificates

The column-side counterpart of the character layer
(`LeanDring/P5/Certificate/Characters/Twin1/`).  Where that layer certifies
*linear characters of `H`* (as `ZMod 25` exponent vectors) fused under `N_G(H)`,
this one certifies *cosets of `H' = [H,H]` in `H`* fused under `N_G(H)`.  The
row/character side and this column/species side are the two different indexings
of the rank-`2724` species table.

`hpData` / `transData` are **untrusted** output of the compiled emitter
`Twin1/SpeciesEmit.lean` (derived-subgroup + transversal computation), re-checked
here by kernel `decide` through total functions only (sift / mul / commutator
arithmetic).

## The boolean certificates (whole-range, one `decide` each)

For each of the 148 subgroup-class reps `H = reps r` with derived-subgroup
candidate `H' = hpData r`:

* `hpWfCheck`      — `H'` is a well-formed echelon pcgs;
* `hpSubCheck`     — every generator of `H'` sifts into `H`  (`H' ≤ H`);
* `commInCheck`    — every generator-commutator `⁅bᵢ,bⱼ⁆` sifts into `H'`;
* `hpNormalCheck`  — `H'` is normalized by `H` (conjugates of `H'`-gens by
  `H`-gens sift back into `H'`);
* `cardCheck`      — `charCounts r · |H'| = |H|`, i.e. `|H'| = |H| / |H^ab|`
  (the cardinality that closes the `H' = [H,H]` squeeze via `card_abelianization_eq`);
* `transMemCheck`  — every transversal element sifts into `H`;
* `transDistinctCheck` — the transversal is pairwise-distinct modulo `H'`;
* `transCountCheck` — the transversal has `charCounts r` elements.

## The fibre split (computed by the `#eval`s of `Twin1/SpeciesEmit.lean`)

On this certified data the `N_G(H)`-orbit count is `2724` and the fibre split of
the orbits **by the order of the coset `hH'` in `H/H'`** is
`{1 : 148, 5 : 2376, 25 : 200}` — *identical* to the character side
(`orbitFibre_by_order`); the raw (pre-fusion) split is `{148, 3688, 1400}`,
again identical to the character raw split by Pontryagin duality.  Neither
matches the `fibreOrder` distribution `{148, 1176, 1400}` recorded in the
external group-library metadata, which is therefore not the fibre of `H/H'` —
raw or fused — on the species side either.
-/

